INSERT INTO feature VALUES('stated-laws','modules','Laws a model proves or admits','modules','implemented','uncommon','mainstream languages','A theory states a law as the path type it is, `law sym : (a : C, b : C) => Path[.A = Bool](eq(a, b), eq(b, a));`, binders first and hypotheses after them, an equation no rule could orient. A model proves it by a definition at that type or, at a host primitive carrier, admits it, `law sym = ~admitted ;`: the admission crosses as the axiom it is, settles `checks` and is listed in the report''s audit. A law a model leaves out the checker discharges (`law-discharge`), and an admission at a carrier the source writes is refused `UnprovenLaw.Admitted`. A stated law is the theory''s generator cell: the globular theory''s associator, modelled by the circle''s paths through `std.math.path`''s associator. A capability scope owes each stated law after the rules, read through its clauses and witnessed by conversion without its hypotheses, and a scope breaking one is refused `HandlerUnlawful` naming the law.','core-checker surface-lowering surface-corpus surface-diagnostics','corpus/model/modules/model-laws.gandr corpus/pathological/modules/model-laws.gandr corpus/model/higher-cells/path-cells.gandr corpus/pathological/higher-cells/path-cells.gandr','corpus/model/modules/model-laws.gandr',NULL);
